import { ApiCopy } from "../../model"

pub fn copy -> ApiCopy = ApiCopy {
  summary: "Create comparison text with Unicode default full case folding",
  purpose: "Use fullCaseFold to compare Straße and STRASSE without their case distinction. Unicode’s default comparison mapping turns both into strasse. This transformation is called case folding. Keep the original text for display and use the transformed value for the comparison you need.",
  reading: "let names the source original and the result folded. folded is strasse while original remains Straße. The same comparison line also folds STRASSE and compares the strings with ==. Both are strasse, so the result is True. Lowercasing alone keeps ß rather than changing it to ss, giving a different comparison result.",
  boundaries: "İ becomes i followed by combining dot U+0307; Σ and ς both become σ. A Unicode scalar is one character-code value. accent scalars is 2 because the input e and combining acute accent U+0301 remain two scalars. fullCaseFold does not normalize the string. The final [] encloses an empty result for empty input.",
  rules: "One scalar can expand into several, as ß becomes ss here. Work is proportional to input and output byte counts. The rules are independent of locale, and there is no argument to request Turkish or another language. std/text.caseFold produces the same result. Calculate any lengths or positions from the converted value.",
  mistake: "The comparison value strasse cannot tell you whether the input was Straße or STRASSE. Retain original if its spelling is needed for display. TypeScript’s toLowerCase changes Straße into straße, so it is not a replacement for fullCaseFold. Normalization, language-specific sorting, and username safety each require their own policy.",
}
